# (#218) The module binding is CONDITIONALLY bound (never, here) and carries
# a boundness bit. The function's call-local binding satisfies `prev of z`'s
# bound-in-scope rule on its own: the first call answers null (one tape
# entry), the second 0.25; the module read after the calls still dies
# "undefined variable 'z'" on both sides.
q is 0
if q == 1:
    z is 9
define u() as:
    z is 0.25
    return prev of z
print of (u of [])
print of (u of [])
print of z
